member.summary:
            Offline fingering for the notes of one hand. Every onset group (single note or chord) gets a set of
            fingers; the whole sequence is optimised with a beam (Viterbi-style) search over an ergonomic cost model:


Parncutt/Jacobs finger-pair spans (): stretch, large-span and small-span costs;

finger rules: thumb or 5th on a black key, 3-4 successions, 4 on black, thumb passing on mixed levels,
              the same finger on two different keys, weak fingers;

second-order (three-note) position-change rules and the 3-4-5 rule;

chords scored over all finger pairs; held notes block their fingers and constrain finger order;

time: rests make stretches and shifts cheap;

chart prior: inside a recognised scale run, the standard scale fingering is strongly preferred.
